  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want any forum link (in a post, the clipboard or a universal link) to open the right screen at the right page and message, so that I never land on page 1 by mistake.\n\n### Scope\n\nPure function `HFRLinkRoute.route(for: URL) -> HFRLinkRoute`: topic (category, post, page, `#t` anchor) from `forum2.php` and canonical `/hfr/<cat>/[<sub>/]<slug>-sujet_<post>_<page>.htm` (slug → category through `ForumCatalogue` aliases), topic list (category, sub-category path, page, filter), profile, MP list/thread, search, unknown/external. Only `forum.hardware.fr` (LESSONS 37, 43).\n\n- Module: HFRParsing · Difficulty: easy · Priority: high · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-020 (#164)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'inbound link router (forum links open the app)'; bug #106 (links keep page and anchor)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `HFRURL.swift`/`CanonicalTopicPath.swift` (SwiftHFR); legacy link handling `MessagesView.swift` (internal topic links), `BrowserViewController.m`\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-095-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-020 (#48, done)\n- LOT-014 (#47, done)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-020 (#164), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-138 (#228); the last lot (LOT-138 (#228)) closes #164.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #127\n- #125\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every link shape present in the fixtures (pagers, quote links, AQ links, bookmarks) routes as tested; unknown shapes are `.external`, never guessed.\n- [ ] Page and anchor are kept (bug #106 regression tests on both URL shapes).\n- [ ] Lookalike hosts, user-info URLs and explicit ports are refused (tests).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-095-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
